WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.311
Privatization timeline.

00:00:02.261 --> 00:00:04.477
How public became private.

00:00:04.477 --> 00:00:13.954
This page documents the thirty-year timeline of Canadian privatization — how public services, infrastructure, and commons were transferred to private ownership and control.

00:00:13.954 --> 00:00:18.102
Healthcare: public system degraded, private clinics expanded.

00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:23.363
Housing: CMHC enabled financialization, REITs captured rental stock.

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:28.795
Infrastructure: Canada Infrastructure Bank blended public risk with private returns.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:33.522
Energy: pipeline politics and carbon pricing reshaped the energy sector.

00:00:33.522 --> 00:00:38.215
Telecom: three companies captured eighty-seven percent of the wireless market.

00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:43.034
Each privatization served institutional interests documented across this site.

00:00:43.034 --> 00:00:47.181
Together they form the economic foundation of institutional capture.

00:00:47.181 --> 00:00:49.556
The privatization timeline.

00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:52.784
Key events from 1995 to present.
